&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About WPP Media&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world-class partnerships – all united by our pioneering agentic marketing platform, WPP Open – we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP Media is WPP&#39;s AI-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;wppmedia.com&quot;&gt;wppmedia.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3263 - Manager, Analytics, UK&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary and Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT OPENDOOR &amp;amp; MGM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At WPP, we&#39;re constantly reinventing the future of creativity, bringing together unrivalled talent, resources and expertise across communications, media, experience, commerce, technology and entertainment marketing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That philosophy sits at the heart of OpenDoor&#39;s partnership with MGM, Amazon&#39;s iconic film studio. For more than a century, MGM has shaped some of the world&#39;s most recognised stories, franchises and cinematic moments. Today, as part of Amazon, it combines Hollywood legacy with the scale, innovation and customer obsession of one of the world&#39;s most influential entertainment companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MGM&#39;s future slate reflects this unique position, bringing audiences a diverse portfolio of theatrical releases and cultural moments. Upcoming titles such as Verity, The Thomas Crown Affair, The Sheep Detective, Masters of the Universe, and The Beekeeper 2 show the breadth of MGM&#39;s ambitions across adaptations, franchises, action blockbusters and original storytelling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;OpenDoor was built to help MGM maximise the impact of these moments. By combining WPP&#39;s talent, capabilities and technology, we create integrated solutions that connect media, creative, data, strategy, commerce and measurement into a seamless operating model. Our role extends beyond campaign execution to helping MGM understand audiences, optimise investment, measure business impact and build long-term cultural relevance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The OpenDoor partnership model is built to deliver next-level productivity through our industry-leading approach to People, Platforms and Process. Drawing expertise from across WPP agencies and disciplines, our teams work closely with MGM stakeholders to unlock smarter, faster and more effective ways of bringing stories to audiences worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By joining OpenDoor, you become part of a team operating at the intersection of entertainment, technology, media and creativity. You&#39;ll work alongside leading industry talent while supporting one of the world&#39;s most exciting film studios as it enters its next chapter, helping shape how audiences discover and engage with stories that define culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are searching for an analytically ambitious, detail-oriented analytics specialist with a genuine passion for film and entertainment to join our OpenDoor team as Manager, Trailer &amp;amp; Campaign Analytics – MGM. This role reports into the Global Director of Insights for MGM and is based in London.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact individual contributor role focused on building and scaling the analytics infrastructure for trailer performance and in-flight campaign measurement across MGM&#39;s theatrical release slate and global marketing operations. You will own the end-to-end setup and delivery of automated trailer reporting systems, working with the team to establish benchmarks, build learnings, and continuously optimize campaign performance through data-driven insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What makes this role distinctive is the opportunity to build measurement discipline from the ground up for two critical areas: pre-launch trailer analytics and real-time in-flight campaign monitoring. You&#39;ll inherit foundational frameworks and collaborate with the broader Measurement team to enhance these with attention measurement, creative A/B testing, and social listening capabilities. You&#39;re expected to identify opportunities for automation and agent-assisted reporting that will scale insights over time — contributing directly to the efficiency and impact of MGM&#39;s global theatrical marketing operation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role operates at the intersection of Paid Media measurement, Cultural Impact analytics, Creative Performance, and multi-platform reporting — translating performance data into clear, actionable insights that directly inform investment and optimization decisions across MGM&#39;s theatrical release calendar. The scope is global with particular focus on key markets, informing measurement practice and learning agendas that shape how MGM launches its most ambitious stories.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Establish &amp;amp; Run Trailer Analytics Reporting&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and operationalize automated trailer performance reporting across all format variants (teaser, full trailer, format cuts) and distribution platforms (YouTube, TikTok, Instagram, Snapchat, Pinterest, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish standardized reporting cadence: 24-hour, 72-hour, and 7-day performance snapshots for all trailer launches across key territories and global markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and build trailer-level KPI frameworks (view velocity, engagement rates, audience retention, CPA, brand lift signals) and communicate performance against pre-established benchmarks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate territory-level performance data to identify which markets are responding strongest to creative approaches, messaging, and format variants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development of automated reporting pipelines and dashboards that enable stakeholders to self-serve key insights between formal reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Integrate Social Listening &amp;amp; Cultural Impact Measurement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy social listening tools (Brandwatch, Talkwalker, or equivalent) to track organic conversation, sentiment, and cultural momentum around trailer launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combine organic social signals with paid media performance to build a holistic view of trailer impact across both channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify emerging cultural moments, audience conversations, and competitive dynamics that materially affect trailer performance and audience receptivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate weekly cultural impact summaries that accompany trailer performance data, providing context beyond metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use these insights to advise creative and media teams on what&#39;s resonating, what&#39;s falling flat, and where optimization is needed pre-launch and in real-time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support Attention Measurement &amp;amp; Creative Testing&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Measurement team to integrate attention metrics (eye-tracking, dwell time, brand recall diagnostics) into in-flight campaign analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with media planning and creative teams to design and interpret A/B tests on creative variants, messaging approaches, and media placements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate attention and creative testing outputs into clear performance narratives that inform mid-campaign optimization and creative recommendations for future campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Benchmark Performance &amp;amp; Inform Strategic Planning&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain a comparative benchmarking framework for trailer and campaign performance, comparing each title against historical performance, competitive context, and similar content archetypes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce quarterly comparative analysis documenting how each title is tracking vs. benchmark, highlighting where performance is tracking ahead/behind and why&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate longitudinal learning summaries that synthesize insights across multiple title campaigns, identifying patterns in what drives trailer and campaign effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the Global Director of Analytics to translate findings into broader patterns and insights that inform MGM&#39;s next-generation campaign planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on investment decisions for upcoming titles based on similar historical performance and learnings from comparable campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build Analytics Infrastructure &amp;amp; Automation Opportunities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to automate routine reporting, data integration, and insight generation — reducing manual effort and accelerating insight delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document data sources, methodologies, and reporting logic to create reusable frameworks for future title campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the broader OpenDoor technology and analytics teams to explore agent-assisted or AI-enhanced reporting approaches that could scale insights over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner Across Functions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work hand-in-hand with Media Planning, Paid Social, and Creative teams to ensure measurement insights directly inform campaign strategy and optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear, accessible reporting that enables non-analytics stakeholders to understand performance and make informed decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the Measurement function in campaign planning and review forums, ensuring data informs decisions from strategy through execution and optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the development of measurement playbooks and best practice frameworks that raise the standard of analytics across the OpenDoor network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate effectively within a matrixed structure, reporting into the Global Lead of Analytics with a dotted line into the MGM Measurement Lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At WPP Media, we believe in the power of our culture and our people. It&#39;s what elevates us to deliver exceptional experiences for both our clients and each other. In this role it will be critical to embrace WPP &amp;amp; WPP Media&#39;s shared core values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be Extraordinary&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;by Leading Collectively to Inspire transformational Creativity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create an Open environment&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;by Balancing People and Client Experiences by Cultivating Trust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Optimistically&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;by Championing Growth and Development to Mobilise the Enterprise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;in marketing analytics, media measurement, campaign analytics, or performance marketing — preferably in entertainment, film, streaming, or media environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Genuine passion for film, cinema, and storytelling&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— you actively engage with cinema, understand audience behavior around theatrical releases, and can speak credibly about what makes trailers and film marketing campaigns work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Demonstrated expertise in multi-platform analytics&lt;/strong&gt;, with hands-on experience building performance dashboards, tracking KPIs across media channels, and reporting on campaign effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Practical experience with social listening and brand monitoring tools&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;(Brandwatch, Talkwalker, Sprinklr, or equivalent), with the ability to translate social signals into business insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Excel, SQL, and data visualization skills&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— you&#39;re comfortable manipulating datasets, building reporting models, and creating clear visual narratives from complex data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience building or owning end-to-end reporting frameworks&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;for marketing campaigns or product launches, including defining metrics, establishing benchmarks, and automating routine reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ability to translate analytical findings into clear, executive-ready communication&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— written, verbal, and visual — without sacrificing accuracy or nuance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Familiarity with media measurement fundamentals&lt;/strong&gt;, including paid media KPIs, CPA/ROI analysis, channel attribution, and performance benchmarking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience working in cross-functional environments&lt;/strong&gt;, collaborating with media planning, creative, content, and strategy teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong commercial instinct&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— you understand how measurement insights drive investment decisions and can connect data to business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Desirable:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on film releases, theatrical campaigns, or tentpole title launches, where rapid reporting cycles and multi-platform complexity are the norm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with marketing automation platforms or analytics tools that support real-time campaign monitoring and optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to A/B testing methodologies and experimental design in a marketing context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with brand health tracking or brand lift measurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI-assisted analytics tools, automated reporting pipelines, or agent-based approaches to data synthesis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active engagement with industry bodies such as the IPA, MRS, or the Media Research Group&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of thought leadership or speaking experience on topics related to media analytics, campaign measurement, or entertainment marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a fast-paced, high-volume environment where you&#39;ve delivered at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LIFE AT WPP MEDIA &amp;amp; BENEFITS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our passion for shaping the next era of media includes investing in our employees to help them do their best work, and we&#39;re just as committed to employee growth as we are to responsible media investment. WPP Media employees can tap into the global WPP Media &amp;amp; WPP networks to pursue their passions, grow their networks, and learn at the cutting edge of marketing and advertising. We have a variety of employee resource groups and host frequent in-office events showcasing team wins, sharing thought leadership, and celebrating holidays and milestone events. Our benefits include competitive medical, group retirement plans, vision, and dental insurance, significant paid time off, preferential partner discounts, and employee mental health awareness days.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP Media is an equal opportunity employer and considers applicants for all positions without discrimination or regard to particular characteristics. We are committed to fostering a culture of respect in which everyone feels they belong and has the same opportunities to progress in their careers. We believe the best work happens when we&#39;re together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That&#39;s why we&#39;ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note this is a UK based role and requires individuals to have the right to work in this location. This position is a 12-month fixed-term contract to cover a period of maternity leave, with a proposed start date of [DATE].&lt;/p&gt;
